    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.3368/le.101.3.092023-0091r",
      "sequence": 1,
      "source_sequence": 285,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "The Trade-Off between Wildlife Conservation and Renewable Energy",
      "title_cn": "野生动物保护与可再生能源之间的权衡",
      "authors": [
        "Brock O’Brien",
        "Nick Hagerty"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "This paper estimates the effect of wildlife protection on wind energy development in the central United States.Federal enforcement of the Bald and Golden Eagle Protection Act increased after a court decision in 2013, raising potential liability for wind developers in regions where eagles are common.We find that counties where eagles are common slowed their wind energy development after 2013 relative to counties with fewer eagles.The costs of forgone wind energy appear considerably greater than the quantifiable benefits from avoided eagle fatalities, suggesting that current policy overvalues wildlife protection relative to green energy.",
      "abstract_cn": "本文估算了美国中部地区野生动物保护对风能发展的影响。在2013年法院判决后，联邦对《秃鹰和金鹰保护法》的执行力度加强，提高了鹰类常见地区风能开发者的潜在责任。我们发现，与鹰类较少的县相比，鹰类常见的县在2013年之后减缓了风能发展。放弃风能所带来的成本似乎远大于避免鹰类死亡所带来的可量化收益，这表明当前政策相对于绿色能源而言高估了野生动物保护的价值。",
