    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.3368/le.101.3.061924-0053r",
      "sequence": 6,
      "source_sequence": 398,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "How Sensitive Are Environmental Values to Payment Card Design in Contingent Valuation?",
      "title_cn": "条件价值评估中支付卡设计对环境价值敏感性的影响？",
      "authors": [
        "Magnus Aagaard Skeie",
        "Henrik Lindhjem",
        "Ståle Navrud",
        "Tobias Otterbring"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Contingent valuation studies of people's willingness-to-pay for ecosystem services are frequently used to inform the social benefit-cost analysis of environmental protection measures.While contingent valuation is generally accepted in this context, response anomalies exist.Drawing on the anchoring-and-adjustment heuristic in psychology and the context effects literature, we examine the impact of subtle design variation on people's willingness-to-pay.In a split-sample national survey of willingness-to-pay to prevent coastal environmental damages from oil spills, different payment card elicitation formats significantly",
      "abstract_cn": "条件价值评估研究常用于评估人们对生态系统服务的支付意愿，以支持环境保护措施的社会效益-成本分析。尽管条件价值评估在此背景下被广泛接受，但仍存在响应异常现象。借鉴心理学中的锚定与调整启发式以及情境效应文献，我们考察了细微设计变化对人们支付意愿的影响。在一项关于防止石油泄漏造成沿海环境损害的支付意愿的全国性分样本调查中，不同的支付卡诱导格式显著影响了结果。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
